   ],
   "spoken": "The King's Indian looks wrong — you hand White the whole centre — but that's the point: you cede it in pawns to attack it later with your pieces from a distance. That's the hypermodern idea.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Hypermodern openings surrender the pawn centre on purpose, then bombard it with pieces."
  },
