   "line": [
    "Re8"
   ],
   "spoken": "The simplest way to lean on e4 is Re8, putting the rook behind the pawn on the open file.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Attack a central pawn with the simplest tool — a rook on the file it stands on."
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 75,
   "fen": "rnbqr1k1/ppp2pbp/3p1np1/8/2PNP3/2N1BP2/PP2B1PP/R2QK2R b KQ - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "f3 is a general weakening move, and here's the concrete flaw: it leaves the bishop on e3 undefended. If we can lever the e4-pawn out of the way, that loose bishop turns into a target.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Every f3 push weakens something — log the pieces it leaves undefended."
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 109.5,
   "fen": "rnbqr1k1/pp3pbp/2pp1np1/8/2PNP3/2N1BP2/PP2B1PP/R2QK2R w KQ - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "c6"
   ],
   "spoken": "We can't play d5 at once, so prepare it with c6 — this is main-line theory, and if White doesn't know exactly how to handle it he's in serious trouble.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "plans": "Follow up with the d5 break to blast open the centre."
  },
